<h2>Signing Up as a Volunteer</h2>
<h3>For New Volunteers</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Complete the volunteer application</strong> — this generates your Level 0 volunteer account</li>
<li><strong>Set your profile</strong> — availability, skills, experience level, any trade preferences</li>
<li><strong>Complete any required training</strong> — safety orientation, platform basics</li>
<li><strong>Get assigned to a Crew Lead</strong> — you\'ll report to someone experienced</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Volunteer vs. Crew Member:</strong> Volunteers are unpaid helpers supervised by a Crew Lead. Crew Members are paid staff. The platform treats them differently — volunteers see available tasks to claim; crew members see assigned tasks.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Profile Setup</h3>
<p>In your volunteer profile, fill out:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>General availability</strong> — when can you work? (weekdays, weekends, both)</li>
<li><strong>Skills &amp; experience</strong> — what can you do? (demo, painting, roofing basics, etc.)</li>
<li><strong>Physical limitations</strong> — any restrictions we should know about? (heights, heavy lifting)</li>
<li><strong>Emergency contact</strong> — who do we call if something happens?</li>
<li><strong>Dietary restrictions</strong> — if meals are provided on-site</li>
</ul>
